`public/sw.js` uses `fetch()` on line 62, but that is the cache-first network fallback inside the service worker's `fetch` event handler — it fetches same-origin assets only (enforced by the `url.origin !== self.location.origin` guard above it) and caches them locally. No external URLs, no analytics, no telemetry. This is the intended offline caching mechanism, not outbound data exfiltration. The file is clean with respect to the product's privacy promise.

